PASS R7 WHY THIS? explains the choice, the dose, where the facts come from (graded) and the record (with Brier calibration); GO DEEPER opens optional depth
PASS R8 I ALREADY GET THIS gives one question from further ahead; right and not guessed → skips to where the idea is used (transfer / far / forge)
PASS R9 DONE stops at once ("Nothing is owed"), returns to the app; the next CONTINUE resumes at the same step, even after a skip
PASS R10 Finishing writes a receipt (what changed, evidence, what comes back) and schedules the hooks 1, 7 and 30 days out
PASS R11 One session a day: after it the door says today is done and nothing more is owed (the stop rule)
PASS R12 Isolation: a whole Renaissance session changes no CNS storage; its own state lives only under "renaissance_v1"
PASS R13 No page errors during the session
PASS R14 Next day: "did you use it?" first, then yesterday's hook without hints (no picture; SHOW ME DIFFERENTLY / DIDN'T CLICK / I ALREADY GET THIS off); a right, sure answer pushes it further out
PASS R15 The next session follows (selection), never two sessions in one day
PASS R16 Life first: exam weekend → shut; 01:00–05:00 → shut (sleep); exam week → a real 10-minute dose (the session continues another day)
PASS R17 Human-life test: when Renaissance takes too much of the week it shrinks itself (≥245 min → 10-min dose) and then rests (≥300 min → shut)
PASS R18 No backlog: after 12 missed days the door offers one ordinary session (one or two warm-ups, normal length) and never says "behind", "missed" or "streak"
PASS R27 A 10-minute day ends with a short receipt and does not close the session; the next day continues from the next step
PASS R19 Kill switches: ?renaissance=off or localStorage "renaissance_off" = 1 → no door, not even booted, and the CNS STOP screen is unchanged
PASS R20 Every task is precise: one right option, every wrong option pre-diagnosed with a named misconception and a repair; every cited source exists; quotations are registered and cited
PASS R21 Every session of every season has the full arc: ≥2 committed predictions (unlabelled items count), a model, two cases compared, near and far transfer, a forge, ≥3 hooks; ≤30 min
PASS R35 Test-wise counterfeit learners fail: picking the longest, shortest, wordiest, punctuated, hedged, jargon-heavy or absolute-free option scores within 0.12 of chance on every item of every season
PASS R22 No open-ended thinking tax ("what do you think", "reflect", "research…"), no links out, no points/badges
PASS R23 The interactive model answers its controls (moving a slider redraws the picture and the numbers)
PASS R24 Every Renaissance button is at least 44 px tall
PASS R25 Right answers sit in different positions (the order is shuffled per item, stable across redraws)
PASS R26 No page errors in content checks
PASS R28 Season 2 follows season 1: six new sessions with unique ids; when season 1 is done the door asks season 2's first question and opens it
PASS R29 Blind comparison: the taste session opens on two versions side by side; a confident wrong pick is kept in the belief ledger (what was held → what replaced it) and WHY THIS? shows it with the capability atoms the step trains
PASS R30 A chart comparison draws both charts from the same numbers, side by side
PASS R31 The boss world is unlabelled: its items name no session and are recorded as their own kind (far transfer, and a belief on record)
PASS R32 Every model in every season reacts to each of its controls; every atom, term, model and picture a step names exists
PASS R33 No page errors in the season 2 checks
PASS R34 On a 360-px phone every label of every figure and every model state is at least 10 px, inside its canvas, and does not sit on another label
PASS R36 Pedagogy governor, level 1: with no record the authored picture comes first; when one kind of picture has preceded right answers clearly more often for this learner it is shown first, except on control days when the usual order is kept; WHY THIS? says which and why; the outcome is logged
PASS R37 Pedagogy governor, level 2: after 20 choices that did no better than the control arm (8/20 vs 5/5), the chooser switches itself off, pictures return to the authored order, and WHY THIS? explains it
